      "translations": {
        "en": "The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon to us before his passing away, which was the last sermon he delivered in Medina until he returned to Allah (Exalted). He gave admonitions that caused the eyes to overflow with tears, the hearts to tremble, the skin to shiver, and the insides to churn. He ordered Bilal to call the congregational prayer, so the people gathered. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came out until he ascended the pulpit and said: 'O people, come forward and make room for those behind you.' He said this three times. The people came forward and some joined others. They looked back and saw no one behind them. Then he said: 'O people, come forward and make room for those behind you.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, for whom shall we make room?' He said: 'For the angels.' The man said: 'Indeed, when they are with you, they are neither in front of you nor behind you, but on your right and left.' The man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why are they not in front of us and behind us? Is it our superiority over them or their superiority over us?' He said: 'You are superior to the angels.' He said: 'Sit down,' so the man sat down."
