      "translations": {
        "en": "Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered the sermon: 'All praise is for Allah, we praise Him and seek His help. We believe in Him and rely on Him. We testify that there is no god except Allah alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. We seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls and the badness of our deeds. Whoever Allah guides, none can misguide; and whoever He misguides, none can guide. O people! There will be thirty liars in this Ummah; the first of them is the Master of Sanaa and the Master of Yamama. O people! Whoever meets Allah (Exalted and Mighty) testifying that there is no god except Allah, being sincere and not mixing it with anything else, will enter Paradise.' Ali ibn Abi Talib (peace be upon him) stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, my father and mother be sacrificed for you, how does one say 'sincerely, not mixing it with anything else'? Explain this to us so we may know.' He said: 'Yes, it is greed for the world and gathering it from unlawful means and being content with it. And there are people who speak the words of the virtuous but perform the deeds of tyrants and evildoers. So whoever meets Allah and has none of these characteristics in him, and he says 'There is no god except Allah', then for him is Paradise. If he takes the world and leaves the hereafter, then for him is Hell.'"
