      "translations": {
        "en": "And whoever befriends an unjust enemy or helps him, the Angel of Death will descend with good tidings of Allah's curse and the fire of Hell, abiding in it forever, and what an evil destination. And whoever bows to an unjust ruler, he will be his companion in Hell. And whoever advises a ruler to do injustice, he will be paired with Haman, and he and the ruler will be among the severest of the people of Hell in punishment. And whoever glorifies a master of the world and loves him for worldly greed, Allah will be displeased with him and he will be in his station with Qarun in the lowest door. And whoever builds a house for show and fame, Allah will carry him on the Day of Judgment to the seven earths, then He will put a fire around his neck which is kindled, then He will throw him into Hell. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how does one build for show and fame?' He said: 'He builds more than he needs, or he builds for boasting.' And whoever oppresses a worker regarding his wage, Allah will nullify his deeds and forbid him the breeze of Paradise, and its breeze is found from a distance of five hundred years. And whoever cheats his neighbor by a span of land, Allah (Exalted) will put a fire around his neck on the Day of Judgment to the seven earths until He throws him into Hell."
